    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not even about a crisis, i'm just talking about the art. i'm trying to write something that actually has weight to it, something that isn't just fake sentiment. i feel like i'm hitting a wall because i'm too afraid to touch the real stuff. the stuff about how everything eventually just fades out or breaks. i want to explore that feeling of the void, but i keep pulling back because it feels too dark. how do i tap into that without it feeling like a cliche?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
