      "content": "To explore difficult themes like impermanence, try focusing on a very specific, small moment where that feeling surfaces instead of trying to address \"everything.\" Instead of writing broadly about the void, describe the texture or sound of something decaying or changing in miniature. Allow the weight of the subject to exist in the observation itself; the most honest moments are often the quietest ones.",
